"Alperin's weight conjecture, Galois automorphisms, alternating sums, and functorial equivalences (https://arxiv.org/abs/2512.07369)\nciteturn1academia12 [wordlim: 200] Published: 10 months ago; Title: Alperin's weight conjecture, Galois automorphisms, alternating sums, and functorial equivalences ... We show that functorial equivalences can offer new insight into the blockwise Galois Alperin weight conjecture (BGAWC).\nTitle: Alperin's weight conjecture, Galois automorphisms, alternating sums, and functorial equivalences\nAuthors: Xin Huang, Deniz Yılmaz\nDate: Mon Dec  8 10:06:59 2025\n\nWe show that functorial equivalences can offer new insight into the blockwise Galois Alperin weight conjecture (BGAWC). Inspired by Knörr and Robinson's work, we first formulate the BGAWC in terms of alternating sums indexed by chains of $p$-subgroups, and we also give a functorial reformulation in the Grothendieck group of diagonal $p$-permutation functors. We prove that these formulations are equivalent. We further show that if a functorial equivalence between a block with abelian defect group and its Brauer correspondent descends to the minimal field of the block, then the BGAWC holds for that block. Finally, we prove that Galois conjugate blocks are functorially equivalent over an algebraically closed field of characteristic zero.--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nAlperin's weight conjecture, Galois automorphisms, alternating sums, and functorial equivalences (https://www.researchgate.net/publication/398476244_Alperin%27s_weight_conjecture_Galois_automorphisms_alternating_sums_and_functorial_equivalences)\nciteturn1search0 [wordlim: 200] Published: 10 months ago; Crawled: last month; # Alperin's weight conjecture, Galois automorphisms, alternating sums, and functorial equivalences ... DOI:10.48550/arXiv.2512.07369 ... Zhou, A reduction theorem for the Galois Alperin weight conjecture, arXiv:2312.02594.\n\n# Alperin's weight conjecture, Galois automorphisms, alternating sums, and functorial equivalences\n\n  * December 2025\n\nDOI:10.48550/arXiv.2512.07369\n\nAuthors:\n\nXin Huang\n\nXin Huang\n\n  * This person is not on ResearchGate, or hasn't claimed this research yet.\n\nDeniz Yılmaz\n\nDeniz Yılmaz\n\n  * This person is not on ResearchGate, or hasn't claimed this research yet.\n\n## Abstract\n\nWe show that functorial equivalences can offer new insight into the blockwise Galois Alperin weight conjecture (BGAWC). Inspired by Knörr and Robinson's work, we first formulate the BGAWC in terms of alternating sums indexed by chains of p-subgroups, and we also give a functorial reformulation in the Grothendieck group of diagonal p-permutation functors. We prove that these formulations are equivalent. We further show that if a functorial equivalence between a block with abelian defect group and its Brauer correspondent descends to the minimal field of the block, then the BGAWC holds for that block. --------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nGalois automorphisms and blocks covering unipotent blocks (https://arxiv.org/abs/2602.14902)\nciteturn1academia13 [wordlim: 200] Published: 7 months ago; Title: Galois automorphisms and blocks covering unipotent blocks ... We go on to study the blockwise Galois--McKay (also known as the Alperin--McKay--Navarro) conjecture for the blocks of almost (quasi-)simple groups above unipotent blocks.\nTitle: Galois automorphisms and blocks covering unipotent blocks\nAuthors: L. Ruhstorfer, A. A. Schaeffer Fry\nDate: Mon Feb 16 16:38:43 2026\n\nIn this paper we prove that a recent condition of Lyons--Martínez--Navarro--Tiep, regarding the field of values of extensions of characters in principal blocks, is satisfied for all finite simple groups, which when combined with their results gives a new characterization of finite groups with a normal $\\ell$-complement for a prime $\\ell$. This leads us to study the distribution of characters in unipotent blocks of disconnected reductive groups and show that this is well-behaved under a generalization of $d$-Harish-Chandra theory. We go on to study the blockwise Galois--McKay (also known as the Alperin--McKay--Navarro) conjecture for the blocks of almost (quasi-)simple groups above unipotent blocks.--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nA reduction theorem for the Galois Alperin weight conjecture (https://arxiv.org/abs/2312.02594)\nciteturn1academia14 [wordlim: 200] Published: 2.8 years ago; In this paper, we investigate the Galois Alperin weight conjecture, which includes Galois automorphisms and group automorphisms in comparison with the original version, and give a reduction to simple groups.\nTitle: A reduction theorem for the Galois Alperin weight conjecture\nAuthors: Zhicheng Feng, Qulei Fu, Yuanyang Zhou\nDate: Tue Dec  5 09:10:54 2023\n\nThe Alperin weight conjecture has been reduced to simple groups by Navarro and Tiep. In this paper, we investigate the Galois Alperin weight conjecture, which includes Galois automorphisms and group automorphisms in comparison with the original version, and give a reduction to simple groups. As an application, we prove the conjecture in some cases.--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nThe Galois Alperin weight conjecture for finite category algebras (https://arxiv.org/abs/2604.06166)\nciteturn1academia15 [wordlim: 200] Published: 6 months ago; We formulate a version of the Galois Alperin weight conjecture (GAWC) for finite category algebras stating that there exists a $Γ$-equivariant bijection between the set of isomorphism classes of simple $k\\mathcal{C}$-modules and that of the weight algebra $W(k\\mathcal{O}_{\\mathcal{C}})$.\nTitle: The Galois Alperin weight conjecture for finite category algebras\nAuthors: Xin Huang\nDate: Tue Apr  7 17:58:57 2026\n\nLet $p$ be a prime, $k$ an algebraic closure of $\\mathbb{F}_p$ and $Γ$ the Galois group ${\\rm Gal}(k/\\mathbb{F}_p)$. Let $\\mathcal{C}$ be a finite category and $\\mathcal{O}_{\\mathcal{C}}$ the $p$-orbit category of $\\mathcal{C}$ defined by Linckelmann. We formulate a version of the Galois Alperin weight conjecture (GAWC) for finite category algebras stating that there exists a $Γ$-equivariant bijection between the set of isomorphism classes of simple $k\\mathcal{C}$-modules and that of the weight algebra $W(k\\mathcal{O}_{\\mathcal{C}})$. We show that the versions of the GAWC for finite groups and for finite categories are in fact equivalent. If $\\mathcal{C}$ is an EI-category, we can give a partition of weights of $k\\mathcal{O}_{\\mathcal{C}}$ with respect to blocks of $k\\mathcal{C}$ and formulate a blockwise Galois Alperin weight conjecture (BGAWC) for $\\mathcal{C}$. We show that the versions of the BGAWC for finite groups and for finite EI-categories are equivalent.--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nAlperin's weight conjecture, Galois automorphisms, alternating sums, and functorial equivalences | Article Information | J-GLOBAL (https://jglobal.jst.go.jp/en/public/202602216423501037)\nciteturn1search1 [wordlim: 200] Published: 10 months ago; Crawled: 4 months ago; # Alperin's weight conjecture, Galois automorphisms, alternating sums, and functorial equivalencesAlperinの重み予想,Galois自己同形,交代和,関数等価性〖JST機械翻訳〗 ... Huang Xin ... Yilmaz Deniz ... http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\n\nPreprint\n\nJ-GLOBAL ID：202602216423501037   Reference number：25P0332077\n\n# Alperin's weight conjecture, Galois automorphisms, alternating sums, and functorial equivalences\n\nAlperinの重み予想,Galois自己同形,交代和,関数等価性〖JST機械翻訳〗\n\n  * Publisher site Copy service\n  * Access JDreamⅢ for advanced search and analysis.\n\nThis is a preprint. See \"About preprints\" page for more details.\n\nAuthor (2)：\n\nHuang Xin\n\nAbout Huang Xin\n\n  * Search \"202650001268368054\"\n  * Search 